\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. And let our bodies part,
\par To different climes repair;
\par Inseperably joined in heart
\par The friends of Jesus are.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Jesus, the corner-stone,
\par Did first our hearts unite,
\par And still He keeps our spirits one,
\par Who walk with Him in white.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O let us still proceed
\par In Jesu's work below;
\par And, following our triumphant Head,
\par To further conquests go.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. The vineyard of their Lord
\par Before His laourers lies;
\par And lo! We see the vast reward
\par Which waits us in the skies.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. O let our heart and mind 
\par Continually ascend,
\par That haven of repose to find
\par Where all our labours end:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Where all our toils are o'er,
\par Our suffering and our pain;
\par Who meet on that eternal shore,
\par Shall never part again.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. O happy, happy place,
\par Where saints and angels meet,
\par There we shall see each other's face,
\par And all our brethren greet.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. The church of the first-born;
\par We shall with them to be blest
\par And, crowned with endless joy, return
\par To our eternal rest.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

